BEHAVIOR t2-acc-init

DESCRIPTION
  Initializes a receive accumulator in a caller-owned buffer: the first 8 bytes
  are a little-endian running-length cell (set to 0); the accumulated request
  bytes live from offset 8 onward. The returned acc handle is a single stable
  buffer the consumer reuses across all recv iterations, so no running state
  has to be carried as a composition value.

CONTRACT
  OUTPUT acc bytes 65536
  GUARANTEES writes_output

HASH 3b21d161

IMPLEMENTATION
  STORE acc 0 8 0
END
